MANUAL CHECKS

A-2/A-3 Contrast, both themes, against the PROJECT'S OVERRIDDEN warm-stone
gray palette (tailwind.config.js — NOT default Tailwind gray; verified the
override is real and the built CSS reflects it):
  gray-50 #fafaf9, gray-200 #e7e5e4, gray-700 #44403c, gray-800 #292524,
  white #ffffff. Sizes: text-gray-700/dark:text-gray-200 is small text
  (12-14px), so 4.5:1 is the bar. Computed (WCAG relative-luminance formula):
    text-gray-700 on bg-gray-50  (light, inline-edit row + its "Starts"/
      "Through" labels + schedule <p>)           = 9.84:1
    text-gray-700 on bg-white    (light, add-form labels/help)  = 10.27:1
    dark:text-gray-200 on dark:bg-gray-700 (dark, inline-edit row)  = 8.18:1
    dark:text-gray-200 on dark:bg-gray-800 (dark, add-form + the month
      input's own fill, which is also dark:bg-gray-800)          = 12.08:1
  All clear 4.5:1 by a wide margin in both themes. For reference the PRIOR
  colors (text-gray-600/dark:text-gray-300) computed to 7.30:1 / 6.90:1 —
  RC3's swap to -700/-200 is a strict improvement, not a regression.
  A-2/A-3: PASS.

