  documents this was deliberately re-picked in BK1 2026-09-08 after
  indigo-500 measured 2.3:1 in dark mode). Computed ring contrast:
    light ring #4f46e5 vs input fill bg-gray-50 (inline row)   = 6.02:1
    light ring #4f46e5 vs card bg-white (add-form)             = 6.29:1
    dark ring  #a5b4fc vs input fill dark:bg-gray-800          = 7.61:1
    dark ring  #a5b4fc vs surrounding row fill dark:bg-gray-700 = 5.15:1
  All clear the 3:1 bar (A-5) by 2x+ in both themes. This is inherited,
  unmodified sitewide CSS (not part of RC3's diff) but its effect on the
  NEW inputs was explicitly what the task asked me to verify, and it holds.
  A-4/A-5: PASS.

