FAILURE

WCAG 4.1.3 Status Messages (AA) / SPEC.md RC3 criterion 7 ("error messages
associated with the field"):
  Traced the actual error path end to end (not assumed): all four add forms
  (income, expense, one-time, big-ticket) POST to handlers that call
  renderRetargetedError(w, msg, 400, "#whatif-add-<kind>-error")
  (internal/handlers/whatif/handlers_income_expense.go:41,164,245,310), which
  sets HX-Retarget/HX-Reswap headers and writes a plain
  `<div class="p-4 bg-negative-soft ...">` with NO role="alert" and NO
  aria-live (renderError, internal/handlers/whatif/handlers.go:1096-1113).
  Verified the actual response bytes from the harness:
    POST /whatif/income {start_month: 2020-01} -> 400,
      HX-Retarget: #whatif-add-income-error, HX-Reswap: innerHTML,
      body: "<p ...>Start month must be Oct 2026 or later (the plan starts
      that month)</p>"
    POST /whatif/onetime {month: 2020-01} -> 400,
      HX-Retarget: #whatif-add-onetime-error, HX-Reswap: innerHTML,
      body: "<p ...>Month must be Oct 2026 or later (the plan starts that
      month)</p>"
  The message text DOES name the field ("Start month...", "Month..."), but:
    - none of the 10 new month inputs' aria-describedby points at the error
      container (they all point at the help <p>, confirmed above) — the
      error is not programmatically associated with the input;
    - the error <div>s (#whatif-add-income-error, #whatif-add-expense-error,
      #whatif-add-onetime-error, #whatif-add-bigticket-error) carry no
      role="alert"/role="status"/aria-live, and #whatif-results (the target
      the inline-edit-row PUT errors swap into) likewise has none;
    - traced web/static/js/base.js's htmx:responseError/beforeSwap/afterSwap
      handlers: they only preserve scroll position and console.error — no
      focus move, no live-region wiring for this path (unlike, e.g.,
      whatif-roth-conversion.js or whatif-spending-optimizer.js elsewhere in
      the app, which DO move focus to `[role="alert"]` on their own error
      paths).
  Net effect: a screen-reader user who submits a month before the plan start
  gets a visually-appearing error box with no announcement and no
  programmatic link from the field they just left — they have no way to
  discover why the add silently "failed" short of manually re-exploring the
  DOM. This is exactly the SC 4.1.3 case in WCAG's own understanding doc
  (inline validation error, no context change, no live region).

  PROVENANCE (git diff bcb6226): the error <div> markup and renderError/
  renderRetargetedError are 100% BYTE-IDENTICAL to master — this exact
  non-live, non-associated error mechanism already existed and is reused
  unchanged by other untouched forms (healthcare, scenario, sync, sweep).
  By the letter of the byte-identical-to-master rule this mechanism itself
  is PRE-EXISTING. What is NOT pre-existing is the pairing: RC3's 10 brand
  new month inputs are new content wired with aria-describedby for the
  FIRST time on these forms (master's year inputs had no aria-describedby
  at all), and RC3's own SPEC.md criterion 7 explicitly promises "error
  messages associated with the field" as this task's acceptance bar. That
  promise is unmet for the new inputs. I'm reporting this as a FAIL against
  the task's own written acceptance criterion rather than downgrading it to
  an observation, because criterion 7 names it explicitly as in-scope — but
  the lead should weigh the pre-existing-mechanism provenance above in any
  CONCEDE/overrule decision; this is not a regression RC3 introduced, it's
  a pre-existing sitewide gap RC3 had the opportunity (per its own spec) to
  close for these fields and didn't.

  Suggested minimal fix (not prescriptive): add `role="alert"` (or
  `aria-live="assertive"`) to the four `#whatif-add-<kind>-error` divs, and/or
  add the error-container id to each field's aria-describedby (space-
  separated with the existing help id) — consistent with the pattern already
  used elsewhere in this codebase (whatif-roth-conversion.js,
  whatif-spending-optimizer.js).

